re_rev_volatility":0.0,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.7379488200593316,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":0.0,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":-0.011486145063514613,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":5.921417253159556,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":0.11471710018359318,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":54.9,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.0844178957003356,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":61.5,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":0.0850387638358403,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":67.5,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.40964153879614074,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":100.0,"_gate_fund_growth":0.07769068847332591,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":77.7,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.017573434620767384,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.019551941509502013,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":25.6,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.00899437013665199,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":85.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.009649999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":6.4,"_gate_insider_buying":1.0,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":100.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Norwegian Cruise Line Holdings Ltd., together with its subsidiaries, operates as a cruise company in North America, Europe, the Asia-Pacific, and internationally. It offers itineraries to destinations, such as Europe, Asia, Australia, New Zealand, South America, Africa, Canada, Bermuda, the Caribbean, and Alaska; and inter-island itinerary in Hawaii. The company also provides features, amenities, and activities, including various accommodations, dining venues, bars and lounges, spas, casino and retail shopping areas, and entertainment choices; shore excursions at each port of call, and air transportation and hotel packages for stays before or after a voyage. It offers its products and services under the Norwegian Cruise Line, Oceania Cruises, and Regent Seven Seas Cruises brands. The company was founded in 1966 and is based in Miami, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John W. Chidsey III, J.D. | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 62 | Compensation: $144,444 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 44K people. Revenue per employee of $221K ranks in the bottom quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 12%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Norwegian Cruise Line Holdings  is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $8.2B market cap on $9.8B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +27% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.2B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 5.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 1.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and within its sector the business captures 2.0\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.4% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 8% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Large open-market insider purchases (net $29.2M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Can NCLH's $325M Savings Plan Drive a Margin Recovery in 2027?","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/nclhs-325m-savings-plan-drive-152800005.html","date":"2026-1